  "boundary": "One fixed noncomputable choice from the current whole function and point. General admissible history-dependent support policies, executable/measurable oracle realizations, Example 2.32, Chapter 2/book completion, full purification and an Exposition Seal remain separate. Proper extended-real losses and global support inequalities are retained without added global convexity or differentiability. The standalone lemma permits arbitrary ambient current x with an actual support; the algorithm starts feasibly. Lean uses zero-based rounds, includes T=0 for fixed bounds, and restricts tuning to positive D,G,T with actual selected-support norm bounds on the same tuned run. Local acceptance does not itself establish exact-head remote CI, merge, main deployment, original PR closure or branch retirement."
